      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Think of a complex signal not as one thing, but as a sum of many pure sine waves stacked together, much like how a chord sound is made of multiple musical notes. The Fourier transform is simply a mathematical tool that acts like a super sensitive microphone, letting you \"hear\" exactly how strong each individual frequency component is within that mix. This decomposition works because any smooth wave pattern can be mathematically broken down into a specific recipe of these underlying frequencies, allowing you to see the invisible structure inside complicated functions.",
